#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:5 eb8e2170cf4345b8a209b21a2ccb1867
msgid "AutoTune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:7 b8810727275d4c3f826f175079a376fe
msgid ""
"AutoTune attempts to automatically tune the Stabilize P, Rate P and D, "
"and maximum rotational accelerations to provide the highest response "
"without significant overshoot. Copter needs to be \"basically\" flyable "
"in :ref:`AltHold mode <altholdmode>` before attempting to use AutoTune as"
" the feature needs to be able to \"twitch\" the copter in the roll and "
"pitch axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:11 6add8b956a9a406fa880d047fba4815a
msgid ""
"AutoTune is not always able to determine a good tune for the vehicle and "
"may result in gains that lead to an unflyable vehicle that may crash.  "
"Please follow the :ref:`Tuning Process Instructions <tuning-process-"
"instructions>` before attempting to use AutoTune. After following those "
"instructions, and have :ref:`evaluated your initial tune <evaluating-the-"
"aircraft-tune>`, should to try AutoTune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:13 b28ce8005da44f4e84a55a6ace1fb22a
msgid ""
"using :ref:`quiktune` before AUTOTUNE, AND setting up the noise notch "
"filtering, see :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering`, is highly recommended "
"in order to get the best tune and avoid possible crashes when using "
"AUTOTUNE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:19 f7fbbdd67a14447ebd3c45f5b9864170
msgid ""
"There are number of problems that can prevent AutoTune from providing a "
"good tune including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:21 304439ab1d144dd2913600edbc25577f
msgid "Strong wind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:22 a317c83144df40aa820ec54f4e1aeebb
msgid "High levels of gyro noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:23 ef14e6c1927e4599a692313226a1a41a
msgid ""
"Non-linear ESC response caused by the incorrect value of "
":ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO <MOT_THST_EXPO>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:24 b94579514fa049b7ad71ecf8492ede10
msgid "Flexible frame or payload mount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:25 ed5d2c89a0924a55a8288b07385c7786
msgid "Overly flexible vibration isolation mount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:26 6485350444a146948597e58a6e239e16
msgid "Very low setting for :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:27 751fe050e4964fff9b5583b50042e2f9
msgid "Overloaded propellers or motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:30 a728418871d74c9088aec573dc999223
msgid "Setup before flying in AutoTune mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:31 9f64c9b693d44a31b00a87860e87552c
msgid "Set up one flight mode switch position to be AltHold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:32 e66892348b7e46ecabca94012067daeb
msgid ""
"Set an RC channel :ref:`Auxiliary Function <common-auxiliary-functions>` "
"switch  to AutoTune to allow you to turn the auto tuning on/off with a "
"switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:34 77998c7f56fa46bfb2a9679a2db48210
msgid ""
"you can also set the AUTOTUNE flight mode as a mode on your flight mode "
"switch to activate AutoTune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:36 a9b53a91b7be426ea43c0e57ff09986d
msgid ""
"Remove the camera gimbal or any other parts of the frame that could "
"wobble in flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:37 6950977bcd5f49ceb5d2b3fffbf6fc47
msgid ""
"Select which combination of axes (roll, pitch, yaw) you wish to tune "
"using the :ref:`AUTOTUNE_AXES <AUTOTUNE_AXES__AC_AutoTune_Multi>` "
"parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:38 34ec80c71424424589497c2d9f1efa92
msgid ""
"Set the autotune's aggressiveness using the :ref:`AUTOTUNE_AGGR "
"<AUTOTUNE_AGGR>` parameter (0.1=agressive, 0.075=medium, 0.050=weak), "
"normally start with the default 0.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:39 b90d7756a06d4515b0cfe385246b0233
msgid ""
"For large copters (with props at least 13inch or 33cm diameter) set the "
"Rate Roll and Pitch filters to 10hz, these are: :ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTT "
"<ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTT__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`, "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTD<ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTD__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`, "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTT <ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTT__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`, "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD <ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:40 bffd6d1419cc4ecb8470598a617e898c
msgid ""
"It is recommended to enable :ref:`battery voltage scaling of PID gains "
"<current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:43 ca333a3e54cb4cd4a8f11d8a700e0700
msgid "How to invoke AutoTune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:44 367ae5b5e41f4e9e97576d932bbc4995
msgid "Wait for a calm day and go to a large open area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:45 e2f1105e96dd4b37a0add14440c11bad
msgid "Ensure the Aux AUTOTUNE switch, if used, is in the LOW position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:46 7b6455b6b4bd4c25b50edd351d333d41
msgid "Take off and put the copter into AltHold mode at a comfortable altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:48 7cb95ee58b4d4ffabfcf6155cbd5b431
msgid ""
"Face the vehicle so that it will twitch at 90degrees from the direction "
"the wind is blowing (i.e. if tuning Roll first, point the vehicle into "
"the wind)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:53 89837464b586486fbe8f6f407790190f
msgid ""
"Set the AUX switch to the HIGH position, or switch to AUTOTUNE mode, to "
"engage auto tuning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:55 95e7f339b8574908b3b1c305e3291cb4
msgid ""
"You will see it twitch about 20 degrees left and right for a few minutes,"
" then it will repeat forward and back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:57 6a651d401db547259de1e9e7f0039320
msgid ""
"Use the roll and pitch stick at any time to reposition the copter if it "
"drifts away (it will use the original PID gains during repositioning and "
"between tests).  When you release the sticks it will continue auto tuning"
" where it left off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:61 2f299d07a7c944b9af90325a517c7e83
msgid ""
"Move the AUX switch into the LOW position, or change flight mode if using"
" AUTOTUNE flight mode, at any time to abandon the autotuning and return "
"to the origin PIDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:63 dfef94efbbb749b9a706d355e54afac9
msgid ""
"Make sure that you do not have any trim set on your transmitter or the "
"autotune may not get the signal that the sticks are centered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:66 6c057b055f3d494bb62713879d474fda
msgid ""
"When the tune completes the copter will change back to the original PID "
"gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:68 5922e2f5c6834311a4c425522730f5cf
msgid ""
"Put the AUX switch into the LOW position and then back to the HIGH "
"position to test the tuned PID gains, or if using the AUTOTUNE flight "
"mode, switch out and then back into that mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:70 8ff9d3b70af241af8991c16d9cf340f9
msgid ""
"Put the AUXswitch into the LOW position, or switch out of AUTOTUNE flight"
" mode, to fly using the original PID gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:71 a374c3c6f6344157b35143aead687b2f
msgid ""
"If you are happy with the autotuned PID gains, leave the AUX switch in "
"the HIGH position, or switch back into AUTOTUNE flight mode and land and "
"disarm to save the PIDs permanently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:74 23b5cf727781427aad7f59be5ecc2d0f
msgid ""
"If you DO NOT like the new PIDS, switch the AUX switch LOW or out of "
"AUTOTUNE flight mode, to return to the original PIDs. The gains will not "
"be saved when you disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:76 f6114db864d84c7f964c5ce87b8252c1
msgid ""
"If you find after performing an AutoTune that the vehicle feels overly "
"twitchy when flying Stabilize, AltHold or PosHold (but ok in more "
"autonomous modes like Loiter, RTL, Auto) try increasing the "
":ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` parameter to 0.25.  This smooths out "
"the pilot's input. Alternatively try reducing the :ref:`AUTOTUNE_AGGR "
"<AUTOTUNE_AGGR>` parameter (it should always be in the range 0.05 to "
"0.10) and try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:80 a196d6dea0bb465f96161bb84dcd2cc8
msgid ""
"If the vehicle feels sloppy after the AutoTune, try increasing the "
":ref:`AUTOTUNE_AGGR <AUTOTUNE_AGGR>` parameter as high as 0.10 and "
"attempt the autotune again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:83 b0c94dec9af643a28f2a6a6c8d79f4c2
msgid "Invoke AutoTune with Position Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:87 ed7ed70bd1ef4a6dbb90e0dcfe236706
msgid ""
"A better tune can often be achieved by invoking AutoTune from AltHold as "
"described above instead of from Loiter or PosHold as described below. "
"Using AUTOTUNE flight mode also has this possible disadvantage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:89 9c2a163112a34aeeb7a920c8d1062cba
msgid ""
"AutoTune performs a weak position hold if invoked from Loiter or PosHold "
"flight modes (as opposed to AltHold) while doing an autotune. If using "
"the AUTOTUNE flight mode, this weak position hold is also used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:95 d75748e81724413b906a73f31d6ee4ed
msgid ""
"The vehicle will gently lean (up to 10 degrees) towards a \"target "
"point\" which is initially set to the vehicle's location at the moment "
"AutoTune was invoked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:96 97dbea93aa244034bcc3538ea2edffd9
msgid ""
"The pilot can reposition the vehicle using the roll, pitch, yaw or "
"throttle sticks.  The target position will be reset to the vehicle's "
"location at the moment the pilot releases the roll and pitch sticks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:97 a4af5ed3d1b54ce48d42b1c4e8f15c67
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The altitude is maintained with the altitude hold controller so the "
"vehicle will attempt to hold its current altitude when the sticks are "
"placed with 10% of mid-throttle. It will climb or descend at up to 2.5m/s"
" (this speed is adjustable with the :ref:`PILOT_SPEED_UP<PILOT_SPEED_UP>`"
" and :ref:`PILOT_SPEED_DN<PILOT_SPEED_DN>` parameters). The acceleration "
"used to establish these speeds is set by "
":ref:`PILOT_ACCEL_Z<PILOT_ACCEL_Z>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:102 c5898f67a3764174a33106ce7f4f6e3c
msgid ""
"To twitch perpendicular to the wind direction, the vehicle may suddenly "
"rotate in either direction up to 90 degrees as it drifts 5m (or more) "
"from the target location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:103 05c5d80b3d584a09868890e117f2bf70
msgid ""
"If there is little or no wind, the vehicle's gentle position control may "
"mean it moves back and forth, ping-ponging around the target point "
"changing yaw each time it strays more than 5m from the target.  In these "
"cases, it may be more comfortable to revert to the simpler AltHold-based "
"AutoTune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:106 10d30ce8fe6248a98731d509e9777b53
msgid "Testing Tune in Other Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:108 9cef07e36c6a41188ba1e7315f334bf3
msgid ""
"The completed suceesfull tune obtained can be tested in any mode, not "
"just the one (ALTHOLD or LOITER) used for entry. A switch can be "
"setup,``RCx_OPTION`` = 180 (AUTOTUNE_TEST_GAINS) that will allow "
"switching between original and autotuned gains in any mode, after "
"autotune has completed. If this switch is setup, but not changed after "
"the auotune has completed, it has no effect. Otherwise if switched high "
"the tuned gains are in effect, if low the original gains. Then they apply"
" to any flight mode and will be made permanent upon the next disarm, "
"based on  switch position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:111 69b7925928c94c748947b307a53c4bb1
msgid "If AutoTune fails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:113 05d2c0fe08264e0ca13ac28d3d5471a0
msgid "If AutoTune has failed you will need to do a manual tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:115 a28130537278412d811752997f185093
msgid ""
"Some signs that AutoTune has been successful are (besides DataFlash logs "
"and Ground Control Station messages):"
msgstr ""

